# https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Security/ExploitCatalogVulnAssessmentRelationship node95
node95 [ shape=none, color=black label=< <table color='#666666' cellborder='0' cellspacing='0' border='1'><tr><td colspan='2' bgcolor='grey'><B>ExploitCatalogVulnAssessmentRelationship</B></td></tr><tr><td href='https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Security/ExploitCatalogVulnAssessmentRelationship' bgcolor='#eeeeee' colspan='2'><font point-size='10' color='#6666ff'>https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Security/ExploitCatalogVulnAssessmentRelationship</font></td></tr><tr><td align='left'>rdfs:comment</td><td align='left'>&quot;Provides an exploit assessment of a vulnerability.&quot;@en</td></tr><tr><td align='left'>skos:definition</td><td align='left'>&quot;Provides an exploit assessment of a vulnerability.&quot;@en</td></tr><tr><td align='left'>skos:note</td><td align='left'>&quot;An ExploitCatalogVulnAssessmentRelationship describes if a vulnerability is
listed in any exploit catalog such as the
CISA Known Exploited Vulnerabilities (KEV) Catalog &lt;https://www.cisa.gov/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog&gt;.

*Constraints*

- The relationship type shall be set to hasAssessmentFor.

*Example*

{
  &quot;type&quot;: &quot;security_ExploitCatalogVulnAssessmentRelationship&quot;,
