# https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/SimpleLicensing/AnyLicenseInfo node242
node242 [ shape=none, color=black label=< <table color='#666666' cellborder='0' cellspacing='0' border='1'><tr><td colspan='2' bgcolor='grey'><B>AnyLicenseInfo</B></td></tr><tr><td href='https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/SimpleLicensing/AnyLicenseInfo' bgcolor='#eeeeee' colspan='2'><font point-size='10' color='#6666ff'>https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/SimpleLicensing/AnyLicenseInfo</font></td></tr><tr><td align='left'>rdfs:comment</td><td align='left'>&quot;Abstract class representing a license combination consisting of one or more licenses.&quot;@en</td></tr><tr><td align='left'>skos:definition</td><td align='left'>&quot;Abstract class representing a license combination consisting of one or more licenses.&quot;@en</td></tr><tr><td align='left'>skos:note</td><td align='left'>&quot;AnyLicenseInfo is
an abstract class representing a license combination consisting of one or more
licenses (optionally including additional text), which may be combined
according to the
SPDX license expression syntax.

An AnyLicenseInfo is used by licensing properties of software artifacts.

It can be:

- a NoneLicense;
- a NoAssertionLicense;
- a single license (either on the
  SPDX License List &lt;https://spdx.org/licenses/&gt; or
  a custom-defined license);
- a single license with an &quot;or later&quot; operator applied;
- the foregoing with additional text applied; or
- a set of licenses combined by applying &quot;AND&quot; and &quot;OR&quot; operators recursively.&quot;@en</td></tr></table> > ] 
