# https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/FunctionalSafety/SafetyContextRelationship node1429
node1429 [ shape=none, color=black label=< <table color='#666666' cellborder='0' cellspacing='0' border='1'><tr><td colspan='2' bgcolor='grey'><B>SafetyContextRelationship</B></td></tr><tr><td href='https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/FunctionalSafety/SafetyContextRelationship' bgcolor='#eeeeee' colspan='2'><font point-size='10' color='#6666ff'>https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/FunctionalSafety/SafetyContextRelationship</font></td></tr><tr><td align='left'>rdfs:comment</td><td align='left'>&quot;Provides functional safety context for an existing lifecycle-scoped relationship.&quot;@en</td></tr><tr><td align='left'>skos:definition</td><td align='left'>&quot;Provides functional safety context for an existing lifecycle-scoped relationship.&quot;@en</td></tr><tr><td align='left'>skos:note</td><td align='left'>&quot;SafetyContextRelationship provides functional safety context for a relationship
between SPDX elements. It enables an existing relationship, such as a dependency
or requirement relationship, to carry a safety integrity level leveraging the existing
relationship types as needed for safety-related use case.

SafetyContextRelationship inherits lifecycle scope from
/Core/LifecycleScopedRelationship so the safety context can be interpreted for a
specific lifecycle phase, such as design, build, test, runtime, update, or
decommission.&quot;@en</td></tr></table> > ] 
